NORMAN-05/DPC Add[endum] 4-A[ specifies] that the structural features must be able to protect passengers from lateral, vertical and head impacts and must be made of stainless steel bars of tubes and enable buoy[ant] material to be[ attached] around it, so that an entire[ fully] loaded basket assembly is able to float.
In order to meet the Brazilian legislation, Reflex Marine has launched the FROG-6, an operational tool that is able to provide a safe option for personnel transfers. The FROG-6 has been subjected to a variety of impact tests to verify its structural integrity and shock-absorbing capability and demonstrated its ability to self-align and float in water, something that is not possible with the traditional rope baskets.
Sandra Antonovic, the company's Chief Operating Officer (C[OO]), says that, "it is a safer method than the traditional rope basket, because it protects the passengers in the event of a lateral or vertical impact, fall or heavy landing. Furthermore, the buoy[ancy] panels enable the device to float and self-align."
